<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-COLLARD HEADS EARLY CHARGE BY PORSCHE.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-COLLARD HEADS EARLY CHARGE BY PORSCHE.</headline>
<dateline>LE MANS, France 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Emmanuel</p>
<p>Collard led Porsche's early charge in qualifying on Wednesday</p>
<p>for this weekend's Le Mans 24-hour race.</p>
<p>Porsche, 14 times winners of the sportscar race, filled the</p>
<p>top three places after two hours of the opening qualifying</p>
<p>session.</p>
<p>Collard, in a Porsche 911 GT, clocked the fastest time of</p>
<p>three minutes 45.490 seconds, followed by Michele Alboreto of</p>
<p>Italy and Belgian Thierry Boutsen.</p>
<p>Leading positions:</p>
<p>1. Emmanuel Collard (France) Porsche 911 GT three minutes 45.490</p>
<p>seconds (average speed 217.127 kph)</p>
<p>2. Michele Alboreto (Italy) Joest Porsche Prototype    3:46.066</p>
<p>3. Thierry Boutsen (Belgium) Porsche 911 GT		3:46.405</p>
<p>4. Max Papis (Italy) Ferrari 330SP Prototype	     3:47.620</p>
<p>5. Eric Bernard (France) DAMS Panoz-Ford GT		3:48.123</p>
<p>6. Jean-Marc Gounon (France) Gulf McLaren GT	     3:48.369</p>
<p>7. Martin Brundle (Britain) Nissan R390 GT		 3:48.376</p>
<p>8. Frederick Ekblom (Sweden) Courage-Porsche Prototype 3:49.005</p>
<p>9. Eric van de Poel (Belgium) Nissan R390 GT	     3:49.764</p>
<p>10. Michael Andretti (U.S.) Courage Porsche C36 Prototype</p>
<p>3:50.142.</p>
</text>
